Calculate the closed form of the following infinite series for a real constant $x \geq 1$:

\begin{align*}
\sum_{k=1}^{+\infty} \left(\ln(k) - \ln(x+k) + \frac{x}{k}\right)
\end{align*}

Given the partial sum:
\begin{align*}
S_n &= \sum_{k=1}^{n} \left(\ln k - \ln (k+x) + \frac{x}{k}\right) \\
&= xH_n + \sum_{k=1}^{n} \ln\left(\frac{k}{k+x}\right) \\
&= x(\gamma + \psi_0(n+1)) + \ln\left(\frac{n!}{(x+1)(x+2)\ldots(x+n)}\right)
\end{align*}
where $H_n$ is the $n$th harmonic number, and $\psi_0(n+1)$ is the digamma function. Using the relationship $\Gamma(x+1) = x\Gamma(x)$ and the limit of the ratio of factorials, find the value of $\displaystyle{\lim_{n\to\infty}} S_n$.

